# Learning Objectives

@body

- Relate allele frequencies to expected genotype frequencies.
- Use p + q = 1 and the Hardy-Weinberg equation.
- Solve the worked population-frequency problems.
- Extend the method to three alleles and X-linked genes.

=== layout: section

# Hardy-Weinberg

=== layout: one-panel
@replaceme

# *Hardy-Weinberg principle*

@body

- States that the frequencies of alleles and genotypes in a population&#8217;s gene pool will remain constant over generations unless acted upon by agents other than Mendelian segregation and recombination of alleles.

- allele
- frequencies
- dominant or
- recessive

- genotype
- frequencies
- homozygous or
- heterozygous

- ?

=== layout: one-panel
@replaceme

# *Hardy-Weinberg Principle*

@body

- HW

- allele
- frequencies
- dominant or
- recessive

- genotype
- frequencies
- homozygous or
- heterozygous

- The [*Hardy-Weinberg principle*]{color=#339966} describes a mathematical relationship between allele frequencies and genotype frequencies and allows the prediction of a population&#8217;s genotype frequencies from its allele frequencies.

=== layout: one-panel

# *Hardy-Weinberg Equation*

@body

- The Hardy-Weinberg equation describes the genetic makeup we expect for a [population that is not evolving]{color=red} at a particular locus
- If the observed genetic makeup of the population [differs from expectations]{color=#5983B0} under Hardy-Weinberg, it suggests that the [population may be evolving]{color=#5983B0}

=== layout: one-panel

# *Hardy-Weinberg Equilibrium*

@body

- In a population where gametes contribute to the next generation randomly and Mendelian inheritance occurs
  - allele and genotype frequencies remain constant from generation to generation
- Such a population is in [Hardy-Weinberg equilibrium]{color=red}

=== layout: one-panel

# *Two Mathematical Rules of Hardy-Weinberg*

@body

- p + q = 1
  - p = dominant allele frequency
  - q = recessive allele frequency
- p^2^ + 2pq + q^2^ = 1
  - p^2^ = homozygote dominant
  - 2pq = heterozygotes
  - q^2^ = homozygote recessive

=== layout: one-panel


@body

![Slide image 1](assets/lect14c-hardy_weinberg_1/image_001.jpg)

=== layout: one-panel
@replaceme


@body

- If _p_ and _q_ represent the relative frequencies of the only two possible alleles in a population at a particular locus, then
  - _p^2^_ + 2_pq_ + _q^2^_ = 1
  - where _p^2^_ and _q^2^_ represent the frequencies of the homozygous genotypes and 2_pq_ represents the frequency of the heterozygous genotype

- HW

- allele
- frequencies
- dominant or
