![Slide image 5](assets/lect14c-hardy_weinberg_1/image_005.png)

=== layout: one-panel


@body

![Slide image 6](assets/lect14c-hardy_weinberg_1/image_006.png)

=== layout: one-panel
@replaceme

# *Apply Hardy-Weinberg*

@body

- [The probability of producing an AA homozygote is p &#215; p = p^2^.]{color=red}
- [The probability of producing an aa homozygote is q &#215; q = q^2^.]{color=gray}
- [A heterozygote may be produced by]{color=#EC9BA4}
    - [an A sperm uniting with an a egg or]{color=#EC9BA4}
    - [an a sperm uniting with an A egg]{color=#EC9BA4}
  - [Each of these events occurs with probability p&#160;&#215;&#160;q, so the total probability of forming an Aa zygote is 2pq.]{color=#EC9BA4}

![Slide image 7](assets/lect14c-hardy_weinberg_1/image_007.jpg)

=== layout: two-panels
@replaceme


@left

|  | *p (0.8)* | *q (0.2)* |
| *p (0.8)* | pp = 0.8 &#215; 0.8 = 0.64 | pq = 0.8 &#215; 0.2 = 0.16 |
| *q (0.2)* | pq = 0.8 &#215; 0.2 = 0.16 | qq = 0.2 &#215; 0.2 = 0.04 |

@right

- The frequency of genotypes can be calculated\:
  - C^R^C^R^\: p^2^ = (0.8)2 = 0.64
  - C^R^C^W^\: 2pq = 2(0.8)(0.2) = 0.32
    - (note\: there are two of these)
  - C^W^C^W^\: q^2^ = (0.2)2 = 0.04
- The frequency of genotypes can be confirmed using a Punnett square
- For the wildflowers
  - 0.64 + 0.32 + 0.04 = 1.

